  "summary": "Iberian and Maghrebi Islamic architecture of horseshoe arches, zellige tilework, stucco lacework and courtyard water gardens.",
  "description": "Under Umayyad Córdoba, Almoravids, Almohads and Nasrid Granada, Moorish builders perfected muqarnas domes, sebka weaves, carved stucco, zellige mosaics and shaded riad courtyards with reflecting pools. The Alhambra condenses its apogee. Islamic geometry — infinite girih star patterns — embodies mathematical transcendence of figuration. Revived in the 19th century (Moorish Revival synagogues, casinos, cinemas) and alive in Moroccan and Andalusi craft today.",
